# Grim Dawn debug overrides - sourced by launch-grimdawn-box64.sh if this file exists.
#
# DELETE THIS FILE to go back to a plain launch. Nothing in the launcher needs undoing.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE STUTTER HUNT FOUND (2026-09-24)
#
# Traversal freezes were vsync. The game ran syncToRefresh=true at 60Hz with triple
# buffering, so DXVK presented with VK_PRESENT_MODE_FIFO_KHR and 4 images. FIFO BLOCKS
# until vblank: a frame even slightly over 16.6ms waits for the NEXT one, and triple
# buffering deepens the queue it blocks on. That is why the probe kept measuring a game
# using almost no CPU while nothing else was busy - it was not working, it was waiting.
#
# The fix is in the GAME's own settings, not here: syncToRefresh=false, tripleBuffer=false.
# Frame rates then reached 95fps, proving the headroom was always there. Measured effect:
# 14 freeze episodes per 420s -> about 4.
#
# Eliminated by measurement, each with the number that killed it. Do not re-run these:
#   shader compilation   the DXVK state cache grew ZERO times across 420s
#   CPU contention       cgroup CPU pressure held at 0.2%; compiler threads starve nothing
#   disk / streaming     only 3% of reads fell inside episodes; no thread ever entered D
#   memory               flat zero throughout
#   wineserver           LESS active during episodes (3.5ms) than outside them (4.8ms)
#   box64 dynarec        WAIT=0 gave 20 episodes against a baseline of 14 - it was WORSE
#
# The launcher's comment claiming BOX64_DYNAREC_WAIT=1 "avoids the input-thread stall when
# Sunshine injects controller state" is therefore STALE. WAIT was never the mechanism.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- The instrument. Comment out when you no longer want the overlay. --------
# "compiler" renders the text "Compiling shaders..." only while compilation is in flight,
# so its ABSENCE during a spike is a real reading, not a missing one.
export DXVK_HUD=fps,frametimes,compiler,pipelines,version

# --- EXPERIMENT 7: stop rendering frames the stream throws away ---------------
# 95fps is wasted work when Sunshine captures at 60 - it burns GPU and CPU and gives the
# capture path more to contend with. maxFrameRate is a LIMITER (a precise sleep), NOT
# vsync: it does not block on the swapchain, so it cannot bring back the freeze above.
# Set it to the streaming fps.
# export DXVK_CONFIG="dxgi.maxFrameRate = 60"

# --- STILL UNTESTED, and it is the ORIGINAL symptom --------------------------
# Whether ANY of this is pad-specific. The hunt began with "smooth with the mouse, stutters
# with the controller", every run since has had the controller connected, and that claim has
# never been isolated. One mouse-only session would settle it.
#
# Also unexplained: the probe twice caught the X server pegged at ~90% of a core while the
# game sat idle, and 7 of the 9 X-hot windows coincided with a stall. Rare, but real, and
# not accounted for by vsync.
